---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Imprint" description="Imprint and buyer commitments for SunHestia — operator status, contact and warranty terms." path="legal">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Imprint</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--c-ink-soft)">Last updated: August 2026</p>

      <h2>Operator</h2>
      <p>
        SunHestia is an independent brand of residential solar photovoltaic and
        battery storage systems, operated by the SunHestia team and serving
        homeowners across European markets.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Registration status.</strong> The operating legal entity behind
        the SunHestia brand is not yet registered. Until it is, the full company
        name, registered office, commercial register number and VAT
        identification number are not available. These details will be published
        on this page as soon as the entity is registered, in line with the
        disclosure requirements of the applicable European jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        General enquiries: <a href="mailto:info@sunhestia.com">info@sunhestia.com</a><br />
        Press: <a href="mailto:info@sunhestia.com">info@sunhestia.com</a><br />
        We respond to most enquiries within two business days.
      </p>

      <h2>Buyer commitments</h2>
      <p>
        Until third-party certifications and the registered entity are in place,
        SunHestia makes the following verifiable commitments to buyers:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Performance guarantee</strong> — solar PV modules carry a 25-year linear performance guarantee.</li>
        <li><strong>Battery warranty</strong> — the LiFePO4 home battery carries a 10-year warranty against defects in materials and workmanship.</li>
        <li><strong>Certified installation</strong> — systems are commissioned by certified installers and are typically completed within a single day for a detached home.</li>
        <li><strong>Right of withdrawal</strong> — for consumer purchases made remotely within the EU, the statutory withdrawal right applies; contact <a href="mailto:info@sunhestia.com">info@sunhestia.com</a> to exercise it.</li>
        <li><strong>Claims and support</strong> — warranty claims and technical support are handled via <a href="mailto:info@sunhestia.com">info@sunhestia.com</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="color:var(--c-ink-soft)">
        This is an interim imprint. It will be replaced by the full statutory
        imprint upon registration of the operating entity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
